  "constraints": "* Category: PYTORCH\n* Time Limit: 200 ms\n* Memory Limit: 128 MB\n* Allowed Libraries: Python standard library, PYTORCH\n",
  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef autograd_l08_sgd_training_step(inputs: list, targets: list, weights: list, bias: float, lr: float = 0.05) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Execute one complete end-to-end SGD training step for a tanh neuron over a mini-batch: forward pass, MSE loss, manual backpropagation, and parameter update.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nExecute one complete end-to-end SGD training step for a tanh neuron over a mini-batch: forward pass, MSE loss, manual backpropagation, and parameter update.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef autograd_l08_sgd_training_step(inputs: list, targets: list, weights: list, bias: float, lr: float = 0.05) -> dict:\n    X, y, w = np.asarray(inputs, dtype=float), np.asarray(targets, dtype=float), np.asarray(weights, dtype=float)\n    z = np.dot(X, w) + bias\n    y_pred = np.tanh(z)\n    loss = np.mean((y_pred - y) ** 2)\n    dz = (2.0 * (y_pred - y) / len(y)) * (1.0 - y_pred ** 2)\n    w_new = w - lr * np.dot(X.T, dz)\n    b_new = bias - lr * np.sum(dz)\n    return {'loss': round(float(loss), 6), 'weights_next': np.round(w_new, 6).tolist(), 'bias_next': round(float(b_new), 6)}\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
